A||||3||Rodney||Clutch arm upgrade||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||06-22-2001||07:34 PM||||I have a new product coming up soon. One I have been<BR>looking at for a few years now. I finally engineered a<BR>design that I can sell for a reasonable price. My first<BR>design was too costly to have CNC machined.<P>As far as I know there were 3 designs for the clutch<BR>pedal. The first design was the aluminum arm with the<BR>large diameter banjo pin and was steel on steel to the<BR>banjo.<P>The second design was an all steel arm but retained the<BR>large pin and was also steel on steel to the banjo. I<BR>have seen the pins on these wear almost all the way<BR>through undoubtedly making a very sloppy clutch pedal.<P>The third design is the small pin and a plastic bushing<BR>in the eyelet of the banjo making it plastic on steel.<P>My new product is a replacement pin designed to replace<BR>the large diameter pin on the steel arm with a small<BR>pin like the late design OEM arm as to utilize a<BR>plastic bushing or my brass bushing. You cut off the<BR>swaged back end of the old pin and hammer the old one<BR>out. This one then just bolts in. The clutch arm will<BR>need to be removed to do this.<P>I am estimating the cost to be around $15. $18 with the<BR>brass bushing included. Plus shipping.<P>I have a couple prototypes on hand if anyone cares to<BR>try one. $10 each and I'll include a brass bushing.<BR>Plus $2 shipping.<P>If it looks OK I'll have some in stock in maybe 3 weeks<BR>or so.<P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-22-2001||09:03 PM||||Rodney, If I read that right you are replacing the pin on the all steel pedal. Is that right?<P>If so this would not help people with the Al arm on the pedal. I always undersood part of the problem with the original is the Al arm get's bent.<P>Replacing the pin on the all steel arm is a great option.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||06-22-2001||09:37 PM||||That is why in my message I said steel arms with the large pin. I would not try to sell to people with the aluminum arms unless they insist. <P><BR>Quote:<P>My new product is a replacement pin designed to replace<BR>the large diameter pin on the steel arm with a small<BR>pin like the late design OEM arm as to utilize a<BR>plastic bushing or my brass bushing. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||06-22-2001||11:52 PM||||I've done this myself to both my cars,and believe me,that's a good price for a sensible solution!||||reg||1
